--single-branch --branch tickets` — the classifier's correctness depends on which ref the fetch advances, which the plan leaves implicit.","ABSENCE: the plan states neither the explicit refspec nor which ref (origin/tickets vs FETCH_HEAD) the equal/behind/ahead/diverged classification compares against."],"finding":"What item 1 specifies a bare `git fetch origin tickets` and classifies the persistent clone against `origin/tickets`, but the codebase's own reconverge (sync.py:232-246) documents that a bare fetch only opportunistically writes refs/remotes/<remote>/<branch> and requires an EXPLICIT refspec (`+refs/heads/tickets:refs/remotes/origin/tickets`) so the remote-tracking ref advances regardless of the clone's configured refspec; the plan does not pin that the classifier reads a ref the fetch actually advances, risking a silent permanent no-op of the behind/diverged branches.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fce8c5d3f13eb082c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"What section, item 1 (\"guard `git fetch origin tickets`\") and item 2 (classify against `origin/tickets`)","norm_id":"n22c26e7b5f3c587e","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["If the ensure-script uses a bare fetch and origin/tickets is not advanced (or is compared stale), the 'behind' and 'diverged' branches never fire and the cross-epoch convergence the ticket exists to deliver silently never runs."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In What item 1/2, specify `git fetch origin +refs/heads/tickets:refs/remotes/origin/tickets` and classify by comparing the local tip against the freshly-advanced `refs/remotes/origin/tickets`, mirroring rebar._store.sync.reconverge; add a shell-integration AC that the fetch advances the remote-tracking ref the classifier reads.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_reli